meta {
  name: consumeProvisionedNewsFeedItems
  type: graphql
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/graphql-api
  body: graphql
  auth: none
}

headers {
  XTM-Hub-Platform-Id: {{platformId}}
  XTM-Hub-Platform-Token: {{platformToken}}
  ~XTM-Hub-Platform-Assertion: {{platformAssertion}}
}

body:graphql {
  mutation ConsumeProvisionedNewsFeedItems {
    consumeProvisionedNewsFeedItems {
      news_feed_items {
        id
        is_deleted
        title
        type
        tags
        metadata {
          key
          value
        }
        creation_date
      }
      available_news_feed_types
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Called by a registered platform (OpenCTI, OpenAEV) to fetch the news feed items provisioned for it since its last
  call. The items are consumed: a second call returns only the newer ones.

  A platform sends either the assertion header or the token headers:
  - XTM-Hub-Platform-Assertion: a JWS signed by the key the platform enrolled (disabled here, enable it and disable the
    token headers to try it). An assertion authenticates one request: sent again, it is refused.
  - XTM-Hub-Platform-Id and XTM-Hub-Platform-Token, for a platform that has not enrolled a key yet.

  The registration must be active and its organization subscribed. Answers UNAUTHENTICATED without valid credentials,
  PLATFORM_ASSERTION_INVALID or PLATFORM_KEY_MISMATCH for a refused assertion, and PLATFORM_TOKEN_REFUSED for the token
  of a platform that enrolled a key.
}
